WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.199
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.499 --> 00:00:08.851
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.151 --> 00:00:15.449
Unit twenty-three: Wildlife Conservation. Today you will describe protection with the passive voice.

4
00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:18.413
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:22.379
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.217 --> 00:00:24.311
Conservation.

7
00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:28.175
Conservation means protecting nature and animals.

8
00:00:28.783 --> 00:00:31.062
Conservation keeps forests alive.

9
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:34.593
Your turn. Say: Conservation.

10
00:00:37.433 --> 00:00:38.551
Conservation.

11
00:00:39.317 --> 00:00:40.318
Endangered.

12
00:00:41.317 --> 00:00:44.152
Endangered means at risk of disappearing forever.

13
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:47.051
The Irrawaddy dolphin is endangered.

14
00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:50.291
Your turn. Say: Endangered.

15
00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:54.204
Endangered.

16
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.032
Habitat.

17
00:00:57.017 --> 00:00:59.341
Habitat means the natural home of an animal.

18
00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:02.240
Forests are the habitat of many birds.

19
00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.154
Your turn. Say: Habitat.

20
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:08.966
Habitat.

21
00:01:09.717 --> 00:01:10.544
Poaching.

22
00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:14.107
Poaching means hunting animals illegally.

23
00:01:14.717 --> 00:01:16.577
Poaching threatens elephants.

24
00:01:17.183 --> 00:01:19.580
Your turn. Say: Poaching.

25
00:01:22.433 --> 00:01:23.400
Poaching.

26
00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.465
Species.

27
00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:30.063
Species means a group of animals or plants of the same kind.

28
00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.986
Cambodia has many bird species.

29
00:01:33.583 --> 00:01:36.259
Your turn. Say: Species.

30
00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.345
Species.

31
00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:42.433
Protected area.

32
00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:46.751
Protected area means land where nature is kept safe by law.

33
00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:49.802
The Cardamom Mountains are a protected area.

34
00:01:50.417 --> 00:01:53.441
Your turn. Say: Protected area.

35
00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.638
Protected area.

36
00:01:58.383 --> 00:01:59.326
Ranger.

37
00:02:00.317 --> 00:02:02.618
Ranger means a person who guards a park.

38
00:02:03.217 --> 00:02:05.065
The ranger stopped the poachers.

39
00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:08.639
Your turn. Say: Ranger.

40
00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:12.559
Ranger.

41
00:02:13.317 --> 00:02:15.339
Biodiversity.

42
00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:19.754
Biodiversity means the variety of life in one place.

43
00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:23.278
Rainforests have rich biodiversity.

44
00:02:23.883 --> 00:02:26.721
Your turn. Say: Biodiversity.

45
00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:31.682
Biodiversity.

46
00:02:32.467 --> 00:02:36.419
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:37.283 --> 00:02:40.235
Visal, why is biodiversity important?

48
00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:44.673
Every species helps nature stay in balance.

49
00:02:45.783 --> 00:02:48.131
How are animals protected in Cambodia?

50
00:02:49.217 --> 00:02:54.107
Tigers are protected in national parks, and dolphins are protected in the Mekong.

51
00:02:55.217 --> 00:02:56.671
Who keeps them safe?

52
00:02:57.783 --> 00:03:01.515
Rangers. Protected areas are guarded every day.

53
00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:04.457
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:05.317 --> 00:03:08.303
Grammar focus: Passive voice (are protected).

55
00:03:08.603 --> 00:03:09.790
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:10.483 --> 00:03:12.854
Tigers are protected in national parks.

57
00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:16.005
The forest is guarded by rangers.

58
00:03:16.917 --> 00:03:19.125
Many species are threatened by poaching.

59
00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:23.517
Use the passive when the action is more important than who does it.

60
00:03:24.283 --> 00:03:28.608
Be careful! Don't say: Tigers are protect in national parks.

61
00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:33.762
Say: Tigers are protected in national parks.

62
00:03:34.062 --> 00:03:36.213
The passive needs the past participle.

63
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.490
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:41.545
Saving Wildlife.

65
00:03:41.845 --> 00:03:45.435
Conservation protects endangered species and their habitat.

66
00:03:46.433 --> 00:03:49.246
Poaching and forest loss threaten biodiversity.

67
00:03:50.233 --> 00:03:52.732
Tigers are protected in national parks.

68
00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:56.255
Protected areas are guarded by rangers.

69
00:03:57.267 --> 00:03:59.417
Rangers help keep animals safe.

70
00:04:00.533 --> 00:04:04.349
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:05.183 --> 00:04:07.485
Tigers are blank in national parks.

72
00:04:07.785 --> 00:04:11.287
A, protected. B, protect. C, protecting.

73
00:04:14.833 --> 00:04:17.123
The answer is A: protected.

74
00:04:18.283 --> 00:04:20.678
The natural home of an animal is its blank.

75
00:04:20.978 --> 00:04:24.619
A, habitat. B, species. C, ranger.

76
00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.433
The answer is A: habitat.

77
00:04:31.583 --> 00:04:33.583
Hunting animals illegally is blank.

78
00:04:33.883 --> 00:04:38.512
A, poaching. B, conservation. C, biodiversity.

79
00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:44.008
The answer is A: poaching.

80
00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.584
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:52.262
Why is biodiversity important?

82
00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:02.597
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:05:02.897 --> 00:05:13.583
Biodiversity is important because every animal and plant has a job in nature. When one species is lost, the whole system is harmed.

84
00:05:13.883 --> 00:05:15.651
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:21.106
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and passive voice (are protected).

86
00:05:21.406 --> 00:05:25.916
Today's value is protecting wildlife. Protect animals and their homes.

87
00:05:26.216 --> 00:05:28.938
See you in Unit twenty-four. Goodbye!

88
00:05:29.238 --> 00:05:31.960
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

